.TH SLEEP 1
.SH NAME
sleep \- suspend execution for an interval
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sleep
.I seconds
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Sleep
suspends execution for
.I seconds
seconds.
.I Seconds
is a non-negative integer.
The wait is taken a second at a time,
so a note ends it within a second.
.SH EXAMPLES
Execute a command
100 seconds hence.
.IP
.EX
{sleep 100; command}&
.EE
.PP
Repeat a command every 30 seconds.
.IP
.EX
while(){
	command
	sleep 30
}
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B cmd/sleep/main.odin
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR sleep (2)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
The exit status is empty, or
.B usage
when the argument is missing, is not an integer, or is negative.
.SH BUGS
The interval cannot be a fraction of a second.
